{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":424099,"duration_api_ms":464223,"num_turns":36,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9b3cb645-4934-4527-ae5e-40bed1d0ec60","total_cost_usd":1.99289455,"usage":{"input_tokens":408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":83415,"cache_read_input_tokens":1700061,"output_tokens":18779,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":83415,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":408,"outputTokens":18779,"cacheReadInputTokens":1700061,"cacheCreationInputTokens":83415,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.8428892499999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":386,"outputTokens":5883,"cacheReadInputTokens":523018,"cacheCreationInputTokens":54322,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1500053,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"The v6→v7 schema migration must rescale the algae half-saturation fields in the save JSON, not just rely on serde aliases. Old saves contain `algae_half_saturation_n_mg_total: 5.0` (\"total mg\" units requiring division by 20). The serde alias on ProcessParams maps this directly to `algae_half_saturation_n_mg_n_per_l: 5.0`, but the code now uses it as mg/L without the legacy /20 normalization. This produces a 20× error in Ks (5.0 mg N/L instead of the intended 0.25 mg N/L), making algae drastically more nutrient-limited in old saves. The migration should rename the JSON key and divide the value by 20 (LEGACY_KINETIC_REFERENCE_VOLUME_L), or alternatively remove the serde alias so old values fall through to the correct defaults via #[serde(default)].","rationale":"Silent 20× behavioral change on any save created before schema 7. Algae growth would be nearly starved of nutrients in migrated saves, producing visibly wrong simulation behavior with no warning."},{"body":"The v6→v7 migration should also rename the plant half-saturation fields (`plant_half_saturation_n_mg_total` → `plant_half_saturation_n_mg_n_per_l`, etc.) in the save JSON and rescale them. Currently there are no serde aliases for these fields, so old saves silently lose custom plant Ks values and fall back to defaults. This happens to give correct values for the standard defaults (8.0/20 = 0.4 matches the new default) but any save with non-default plant Ks values will silently reset.","rationale":"Silent data loss for saves with customized plant nutrient parameters. While the default case works by coincidence (8.0/20 = 0.4), this is fragile and incorrect for any non-standard configuration."},{"body":"The pre-existing test `substrate_deep_area_scales_with_depth_and_kind` (crates/tank_core/tests/habitat_registry.rs:227) is broken by the substrate refactor. It creates a CoarsePorous layer with `..SubstrateLayerState::default()`, which sets `colonizable_area_factor = 0.5` (InertSand default), but the expected calculation uses 0.9 (CoarsePorous factor). With the new code using `resolved_colonizable_area_factor()` instead of `kind.colonizable_area_factor()`, the test expects `footprint * 1.5 * 0.9` but gets `footprint * 1.5 * 0.5`. Fix by explicitly setting `colonizable_area_factor: SubstrateKind::CoarsePorous.default_colonizable_area_factor()` on the test layer (and similarly for any other test layers that override kind).","rationale":"Compilation is already blocked by an unrelated snapshot.rs error, but once that's fixed this test will fail. The test was correct before the refactor but now tests against dead behavior."},{"body":"The `legacy_process_param_normalization` function in crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs no longer handles the old algae field names (`algae_half_saturation_n_mg_total`, `algae_half_saturation_p_mg_total`), but the `ProcessParamsPreset` struct still has serde aliases for them. Any user-created preset TOML referencing the old names will have the value loaded via alias but not normalized, producing a 20× error in the preset pathway as well. Either remove the serde aliases from ProcessParamsPreset (breaking old custom presets cleanly) or keep the old names in the normalization function so they get /20 treatment.","rationale":"Custom presets using old field names would silently produce wrong algae nutrient limitation values. The serde alias and normalization function are inconsistent — one accepts the old name while the other ignores it."}],"summary":"Reviewed the full diff (save.rs, substrate.rs, process.rs, presets.rs, algae_growth.rs, plant_growth.rs, chemistry.rs, shrimp.rs, biology.rs, tests). The substrate colonizable_area_factor promotion and CO2 KLA refactor are structurally sound. However, the process-parameter rename from legacy \\\"total mg\\\" fields to concentration-based fields has four correctness/compatibility gaps: (1) the v6→v7 migration doesn't rescale algae Ks values, causing a 20× error via serde alias on old saves; (2) plant Ks fields silently reset to defaults in old saves due to missing aliases/migration; (3) a pre-existing test is broken because SubstrateLayerState::default() now carries a fixed factor that doesn't match the overridden kind; (4) the preset normalization function and serde aliases are inconsistent for old algae field names."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"1d42f3f6-0762-4ed5-b579-0305525e8829"}
